            <ArticleTitle>Isolation of an unusual [Cu6] nanocluster through sequential addition of copper(i) to a polynucleating ligand.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2077-2080</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6dt04703c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Addition of 2 equiv. of CuI to a [Cu]4 multimetallic complex results in cluster formation leading to the isolation of a rare bicapped tetrahedral [Cu6I2] cluster that is stabilised by two conformationally constrained polynucleating ligands.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
